<article class="env-lemma" id="03YX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03YX">Lemma <span data-tag="03YX">59.20.3</span>.</a> Let $\tau \in \{ {\acute{e}tale}, Zariski\} $. If $\mathcal{F}$ is an abelian sheaf defined on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau $, then the cohomology groups of $\mathcal{F}$ over $S$ agree with the cohomology groups of $\mathcal{F}|_{S_\tau }$ over $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Topologies, Lemmas <a href="/tag/020Z" data-tag="020Z">34.3.14</a> and <a href="/tag/021G" data-tag="021G">34.4.14</a> the functors $S_\tau \to (\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau $ satisfy the hypotheses of Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/00XU" data-tag="00XU">7.21.8</a>. Hence our lemma follows from Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/03YU" data-tag="03YU">21.7.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>